  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed extensions, by reason of their excessive size and scale, and siting along the shared boundary with No. 42 North Drive (D1), would result in a development that is unduly overbearing and would cause an unacceptable loss of daylight, sunlight and outlook to the neighbouring property, contrary to the Residential Extension Guidelines, and Local Plan Policies CC2 (Urban Design and Architecture) and SC7 (Residential Extensions and Alterations), and the principles of the National Planning Policy Framework.",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposed extensions, by virtue of their excessive size, bulk, projection and cumulative massing in relation to the original dwelling, would fail to appear subordinate or proportionate to the host property. Given the site's prominent corner location, the proposed extensions would project awkwardly toward the adjoining footpath and, when combined with the existing additions to the property, would create an unduly dominant, visually incongruous and unbalanced form of development. This would harm the character and appearance of the host dwelling, the adjoining terraced properties and the wider street scene. The proposal therefore would fail to conserve or enhance the character of the area, contrary to Policies CC1 (Context and Character), CC2 (Urban Design and Architecture) and SC7 (Residential Extensions and Alterations) of the adopted Local Plan."
  ],
